From bbcc596ff1f3b1e7d3351947c9a9e441ab825be7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vigorouscoding <kai.schwaiger@structr.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Feb 2017 17:28:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bugfix: Correctly respects configuration switch
 `application.filesystem.unique.paths` when renaming files/folders


diff --git a/structr-ui/src/main/java/org/structr/web/entity/AbstractFile.java b/structr-ui/src/main/java/org/structr/web/entity/AbstractFile.java
index 5bb005d96..ab8131d11 100644
--- a/structr-ui/src/main/java/org/structr/web/entity/AbstractFile.java
+++ b/structr-ui/src/main/java/org/structr/web/entity/AbstractFile.java
@@ -92,7 +92,12 @@ public class AbstractFile extends LinkedTreeNode<FileChildren, FileSiblings, Abs
 	@Override
 	public boolean onModification(final SecurityContext securityContext, final ErrorBuffer errorBuffer, final ModificationQueue modificationQueue) throws FrameworkException {

-		final boolean valid = validatePath(securityContext, errorBuffer);
+		boolean valid = true;
+
+		if (validatePathUniqueness) {
+			valid = validatePath(securityContext, errorBuffer);
+		}
+
 		return valid && super.onModification(securityContext, errorBuffer, modificationQueue);
 	}

-- 
2.48.1

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
final boolean valid = validatePath(securityContext, errorBuffer);
Reason:
This line unconditionally calls `validatePath()` in the `onModification` method of `AbstractFile`, without checking the `validatePathUniqueness` flag first. This flag is meant to reflect the `application.filesystem.unique.paths` configuration setting, which controls whether path uniqueness should be enforced. Because the validation call is not gated by this flag, path uniqueness validation is always performed during rename operations, even when the configuration explicitly disables it, leading to incorrect validation behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
boolean valid = true;
if (validatePathUniqueness) {
    valid = validatePath(securityContext, errorBuffer);
}
Reason:
The fix introduces a conditional check on the `validatePathUniqueness` flag before calling `validatePath()`. The `valid` variable is initialized to `true` by default, and `validatePath()` is only invoked if `validatePathUniqueness` is `true`. This ensures that path uniqueness validation is skipped entirely when the `application.filesystem.unique.paths` configuration switch is disabled, correctly respecting the configuration setting during rename operations on files/folders.

